{"reference":"Genesis 9","book":"Genesis","chapter":9,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"A flood comparison","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"A Neo-Assyrian tablet copy preserves the Standard Babylonian Epic's account of Uta-napishti surviving a divinely sent flood. The comparison reaches through Genesis 6–9, including preservation of life, birds, landing, and post-flood sacrifice. These shared motifs support comparison, but they do not establish direct borrowing.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_genesis_009_1a7776cc33516570ff0e3ea8"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}
